{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the problem and submitted the mitigation. The submission returned a 200 \"Submission received\".\n\n**Root cause:** The `frontend` deployment was pinned to `kind-worker2` and `recommendation` to `kind-worker`. The frontend's connections to recommendation timed out (`ETIMEDOUT` to the service IP), so `/api/recommendations` returned 504s after about 15 seconds. All the feature flags were off, and nothing else was broken. I didn't find why traffic between those two nodes failed.\n\n**Fix:** I removed the `nodeSelector` from both deployments. The pods rescheduled onto other nodes (`frontend` on `kind-worker`, `recommendation` on `kind-worker3`).\n\n**Check after the fix:** Through `frontend-proxy`, `/api/recommendations` returned 200 in about 12 ms on three tries, and the home page returned 200. I only ran this check once, a few seconds after the rollout, so I haven't seen it hold over a longer period."}}
